architecture. Computer Vision and Image Understanding, 203(2021)103125. （CCF B期刊）\n\n22. Usman Ali, Bayram Bayramli, Tamam Alsarhan, Hongtao Lu. A lightweight network for monocular depth estimation with decoupled body and edge supervision. Image and Vision Computing, 113 (2021) 104261.\n\n23. Luay Alawneh, Tamam Alsarhan, Mohammad Al‑Zinati, Mahmoud Al‑Ayyoub, Yaser Jararweh, Hongtao Lu. Enhancing human activity recognition using deep learning and time series augmented data. Journal of Ambient Intelligence and Humanized Computing (2021) 12:10565–10580. https://doi.org/10.1007/s12652-020-02865-4\n\n24. Yiru Zhao, Hongtao Lu. Neighbor similarity and soft-label adaptation for unsupervised cross-dataset person re-identification. Neurocomputing, 388 (2020) 246-254.\n\n会议论文：\n\n2025\n\n1. Yanbiao Ji, Yue Ding, Dan Luo, Chang Liu, Yuxiang Lu, Xin Xin, Hongtao Lu. How Does Topology Bias Distort Message Passing? A Dirichlet Energy Perspective. NeurIPS, 2025.\n\n2. Suizhi Huang, Xingyi Yang, Hongtao Lu, Xinchao Wang. Few-shot implicit function generation via equivariance. CVPR, 2025.\n\n3. Mei Li, Yuxiang Lu, Qinyan Dai, Suizhi Huang, Yue Ding, Hongtao Lu. BECAME:BayEsian Continual Learning with Adaptive Model Merging. ICML, 2025.\n\n4. Shaokai Wu, Yuxiang Lu, Yapan Guo, Wei Ji, Suizhi Huang, Fengyu Yang, Shalayiding Sirejiding, Qichen He, Jing Tong, Yanbiao Ji, Yue Ding, Hongtao Lu. Discretized Gaussian Representation for Tomographic Reconstruction. ICCV 2025.\n\n5. Shalayiding Sirejiding, Yue Ding, Yuxiang Lu, Xinyi Hou, Shaokai Wu, Qichen He, Chunlin Wang, Wenqiang Guo, Hongtao Lu. CLIP-MT: Multi-Modal Knowledge-Driven Adaptive Scale Feature Allocation for Multi-Task Dense Prediction. ACM Multimedia 2025.\n\n6. Yanbiao Ji, Dan Luo, Chang Liu, Shaokai Wu, Jing Tong, Qichen He, Deyi Ji, Hongtao Lu, Yue Ding. Generating Negative Samples for Multi-Modal Recommendation. ACM Multimedia 2025.\n\n7. Shaokai Wu, Yapan Guo, Yanbiao Ji, Jing Tong, Yuxiang Lu, Mei Li, Suizhi Huang, Yue Ding, Hongtao Lu. MORE: Multi-Organ Medical Image REconstruction Dataset. ACM Multimedia 2025.\n\n8. Yanbiao Ji, Chang Liu, Xin Chen, Dan Luo, Mei Li, Yue Ding, Wenqing Lin, Hongtao Lu. From Anchors to Answers: A Novel Node Tokenizer for Integrating Graph Structure into Large Language Models. CIKM’25, 2025.\n\n9. Yue Ding, Yanbiao Ji, Xun Cai, Xin Xin, Yuxiang Lu, Suizhi Huang, Chang Liu, Xiaofeng Gao, Tsuyoshi Murata, Hongtao Lu. Towards Personalized Federated Multi-Scenario Multi-Task Recommendation. WSDM 2025.\n\n资助项目\n\n- 国家自然科学基金面上项目: 面向多任务图像编辑的轻量级深度神经网络研究，No. 62176155, 2022.01-2025.12, 主持。\n\n- 国家自然科学基金面上项目：深度神经网络压缩及其应用研究,No.61772330,2018.01-2021.12，主持。\n\n获奖信息\n\n1. 上海市自然科学奖二等奖，2010年，排名1\n\n学术服务\n\n中国图像图形学报编委\n\n数据采集语处理编委\n\nIEEE PRML的Technical committee\n\nICLR会议的程序委员会成员\n\nIEEE CVPR会议的程序委员会成员\n\nAAAI会议的程序委员会成员\n\nACM SIGIR会议的程序委员会成员\n\nACM SIGIR-AP会议的程序委员会成员\n\nACM CIKM会议的程序委员会成员\n\nACM Web Conference (WWW)程序委员会成员	\N
8b7d900f-d15f-473b-8b08-6b55bdb0bcde	c433cf66-4f87-4389-b4e2-73456516f033	https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jiaoshiml/lyubaoliang.html	https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jiaoshiml/lyubaoliang.html	5e15c2dc39a29edb64d7b92992d4f72d	2026-10-22 09:59:30.778735+00	200	static	utf-8	1ea85e50a257cd8b2099e91112565994	# 吕宝粮-上海交通大学计算机学院（网络空间安全学院、密码学院）\n\n[使用jAccount登录](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/user/jaccount_login.html)\n\n[English](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/en)\n\n师资队伍\n\n- ## [教师名录](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jiaoshiml.html)\n\n- ## [院士学者](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/lyys.html)\n\n- ## [国家级人才](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/gjjrc.html)\n\n- ## [兼职和双聘教师](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jzhesp.html)\n\n- ## [退休教师](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/txjiaoshi.html)\n\n- ## [人才招聘](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/rczp.html)\n\n教师名录\n\n吕宝粮\n\n长聘教授\n\n电话：021-34204421\n\n邮箱：bllu@sjtu.edu.cn\n\n所在研究所：通用人工智能研究所\n\n个人主页：[https://bcmi.sjtu.edu.cn/~blu/](https://bcmi.sjtu.edu.cn/~blu/)\n\n个人简介\n\nPh.D., IEEE Fellow, Professor, Directors\nCenter for Brain-like Computing and Machine Intelligence\nDepartment of Computer Science and Engineering\nShanghai Jiao Tong University\nKey Laboratory of Shanghai Commission for Intelligent Interaction and Cognitive Engineering\nShanghai Jiao Tong University\nCenter for Brain-Machine Interface and Neuromodulation, RuiJin Hospital, Shanghai Jiao Tong University School of Medicine\nRuiJin-MiHoYo Laboratory, RuiJin Hospital, Shanghai Jiao Tong University School of Medicine\n\n教育背景\n\nI received the B.S. degree in instrument and control engineering from Qingdao University of Science and Technology, China, in 1982, the M. S. degree in computer science and engineering from Northwestern Polytechnical University, Xi'an, China, in 1989, and the Dr. Eng. degree in electrical engineering from Kyoto University, Kyoto, Japan, in 1994.\n\n工作履历\n\nFrom 1982 to 1986, I was with the Qingdao University of Science and Technology.\n\nFrom April 1994 to March 1999, I was a Frontier Researcher at the Bio-Mimetic Control Research Center, the Institute of Physical and Chemical Research (RIKEN), Nagoya, Japan.\n\nFrom April 1999 to August 2002, I was a Research Scientist at the RIKEN Brain Science Institute, Wako, Japan.\n\nSince August 2002, I have been a full professor at the School of Computer Science, Shanghai Jiao Tong University, China.\n\nCenter for Brain-Machine Interface and Neuromodulation, RuiJin Hospital, Shanghai Jiao Tong University School of Medicine\n\n教授课程\n\n- Neural Network Theory and Applications\n\n- Parallel Machine Learning with Application to Large-Scale Data Mining\n\n论文发表\n\n2025\n\n- Wei-Bang Jiang, Yansen Wang, Bao-Liang Lu, Dongsheng Li, NeuroLM: A Universal Multi-task Foundation Model for Bridging the Gap between Language and EEG Signals.In The Thirteenth International Conference on Learning Representations, 2025. [[pdf]](https://openreview.net/pdf?id=Io9yFt7XH7)\n\n- Hao-Long Yin, Wei-Long Zheng, Bao-Liang Lu, STAR: A Spatial-Temporal Autoencoder for EEG Restoration in Emotion Recognition, Proc. of ICASSP 2025.\n\n- Jian-Ming Zhang, Wei-Bang Jiang, Wei-Long Zheng, Bao-Liang Lu, Multi-Scale Attention-Based Dense Spatial-Temporal Model for Emotion Induction in Response to Olfactory Stimuli, Proc. of ICASSP 2025.\n\n- Ziyi Li, Wei-Long Zheng, Bao-Liang Lu, Gram: A Large-Scale General EEG Model for Raw Data Classification and Restoration Tasks, Proc. of ICASSP 2025.\n\n- Haiqing Hu, Hanwen Shi, Bao-Liang Lu, Wei-Long Zheng, Multi-Source Multi-Target Domain Similarity Network for Cross-Cultural EEG Emotion Recognition, Proc. of ICASSP 2025.\n\n- David Edwin Carlson, Ricardo Chavarriaga, Yiling Liu, Fabien Lotte, Bao-Liang Lu, The NERVE-ML (Neural Engineering Reproducibility and Validity Essentials for Machine Learning) Checklist: Ensuring Machine Learning Advances Neural Engineering, Journal of Neural Engineering.\n\n- Huan Liu, Shusen Yang, Yuzhe Zhang, Mengze Wang, Fanyu Gong, Chengxi Xie, Guanjian Liu, Zejun Liu, Yong-Jin Liu, Bao-Liang Lu, Dali