0615bec5-1c17-421a-89d8-c346e15a3e88	8fba1b29-4307-42cb-95dd-3e7bacf3ab38	https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jiaoshiml/tushikui.html	https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jiaoshiml/tushikui.html	e881fd969ed970d9358a6b29ca482b59	2026-10-22 10:00:25.071959+00	200	static	utf-8	3c2f6ddedbb2672d945998699e55150e	# 涂仕奎-上海交通大学计算机学院（网络空间安全学院、密码学院）\n\n[使用jAccount登录](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/user/jaccount_login.html)\n\n[English](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/en)\n\n师资队伍\n\n- ## [教师名录](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jiaoshiml.html)\n\n- ## [院士学者](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/lyys.html)\n\n- ## [国家级人才](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/gjjrc.html)\n\n- ## [兼职和双聘教师](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jzhesp.html)\n\n- ## [退休教师](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/txjiaoshi.html)\n\n- ## [人才招聘](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/rczp.html)\n\n教师名录\n\n涂仕奎\n\n长聘副教授\n\n邮箱：tushikui@sjtu.edu.cn\n\n地址：东川路800号电院3号楼541\n\n所在研究所：通用人工智能研究所\n\n个人主页：[https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/~tushikui/](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/~tushikui/)\n\n个人简介\n\n涂仕奎，上海交通大学计算机学院长聘副教授、博导，国家级青年人才。北大数学本科、香港中文大学计算机博士，UMassMed博后。长期从事机器学习、及其与生化医药交叉研究，发表论文100余篇，含Science、Cell正刊、Nature子刊，以及NeurIPS、ICML等人工智能领域CCF-A类会议。获吴文俊人工智能科学技术奖自然科学奖二等奖(第3完成人)、华为云与计算先锋教师、省部级校级教学成果奖4项等。主持和参与国家基金委、科技部、上海市科委等人工智能领域项目多项。\n\n教育背景\n\n2002-2006，北京大学，数学科学学院，本科\n\n2006-2012，香港中文大学，计算机科学与工程系，博士\n\n工作履历\n\n2012-2016, 美国麻省大学[伍斯特校区]（医学院），博士后\n\n2017-2023，上海交通大学，计算机科学与工程系，长聘教轨副教授\n\n2023-至今，上海交通大学，计算机学院（计算机科学与工程系），长聘副教授\n\n教授课程\n\nCS3308 机器学习（本科生课程）\n\nCS2601 线性优化与凸优化（本科生课程）\n\nCS7315 基因组学之大数据学习（研究生课程）\n\n论文发表\n\n部分代表论文：\n\n1. Donglei Zhang#, Shikui Tu#, Michael Stubna, Wei-Sheng Wu, Wei-Che Huang, Zhiping Weng, Heng-Chi Lee. "The rules for piRNA targeting reveal resistance of endogenous genes to piRNA silencing in C. elegans." Science, Vol. 359, Issue 6375, pp. 587-592, 2 February 2018 (#co-first author)\n\n2. Dengwei Zhao, Shikui Tu*, Lei Xu*. "SeeA*: Efficient Exploration-Enhanced A* Search by Selective Sampling", The Thirty-eighth Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2024), Dec. 10-15, 2024 (Oral paper, acceptance rate: 61/15671=0.39%) (* corresponding author)\n\n3. Dengwei Zhao, Shikui Tu*, and Lei Xu*, "Efficient Learning for AlphaZero via Path Consistency". In Proceedings of the 39th International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML), Baltimore, Maryland, USA, PMLR 162:26971-26981, 2022\n\n4. Hao Qian, Wenjing Huang, Shikui Tu*, and Lei Xu*. "KGDiff: towards explainable target-aware molecule generation with knowledge guidance", Briefings in Bioinformatics (BIB), Volume 25, Issue 1, bbad435, January 2024\n\n5. Peiying Li, Yongchang Liu, Jiafeng Zhou, Shikui Tu*, Bing Zhao, Jieqing Wan, Yunjun Yang*, and Lei Xu*. “A deep learning method for end-to-end prediction of intracranial aneurysm rupture risk”. Patterns 4, 100709, May 12, 2023\n\n更多已发表论文请见：\n\n[https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=Yewd61kAAAAJ&hl=en](https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=Yewd61kAAAAJ&hl=en)\n\n获奖信息\n\n2024 获吴文俊人工智能科学技术奖自然科学奖二等奖(第3完成人)\n\n2022 获上海市计算机学会教学成果奖一等奖（排位第3）\n\n2022 获上海市教学成果奖一等奖（排位第7）\n\n2021 获上海交通大学教学成果奖特等奖（排位第6）\n\n2020 获华为先锋教师奖\n\n2018 获教育部-华为产学合作协同育人项目“新工科建设项目(A类) ”《机器学习类课程建设与实践》（排位第2），结题获评优秀\n\n2018 获评第十四批国家中组部青年千人	\N
fa30952c-9eb5-4002-8516-93687d9c8c77	c7c0fafd-0752-4ff8-8fe5-d072abcc34a8	https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jiaoshiml/wangrui.html	https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jiaoshiml/wangrui.html	2209441a3132aab958c5dd52472a2288	2026-10-22 10:00:53.264977+00	200	static	utf-8	da5d128e951abc39e22239e785a2df59	# 王瑞-上海交通大学计算机学院（网络空间安全学院、密码学院）\n\n[使用jAccount登录](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/user/jaccount_login.html)\n\n[English](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/en)\n\n师资队伍\n\n- ## [教师名录](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jiaoshiml.html)\n\n- ## [院士学者](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/lyys.html)\n\n- ## [国家级人才](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/gjjrc.html)\n\n- ## [兼职和双聘教师](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jzhesp.html)\n\n- ## [退休教师](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/txjiaoshi.html)\n\n- ## [人才招聘](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/rczp.html)\n\n教师名录\n\n王瑞\n\n长聘教轨副教授\n\n邮箱：wangrui12@sjtu.edu.cn\n\n所在研究所：通用人工智能研究所\n\n个人主页：[https://wangruinlp.github.io/](https://wangruinlp.github.io/)\n\n个人简介\n\nI have been a faculty member at Shanghai Jiao Tong University (SJTU) since 2021. From 2016 to 2020, I worked as a researcher at the National Institute of Information and Communications Technology (NICT) in Japan, following an internship there in 2013. I am deeply grateful to my senseis at NICT—[Masao Utiyama](https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=artIO6gAAAAJ&hl=en&oi=ao) and [Eiichiro Sumita](https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=AgC7dTQAAAAJ&hl=en)—for their invaluable guidance, support, and inspiration throughout my time in Japan. From 2012 to 2016, I pursued a joint Ph.D. between SJTU and the French National Centre for Scientific Research (CNRS), under the supervision of [Hai Zhao](https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=H6vHKJoAAAAJ&hl=zh-CN), [Bao-Liang Lu](https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=709il6EAAAAJ&hl=zh-CN), and [Sabine Ploux](https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Sabine-Ploux). Prior to my doctoral studies, I studied and worked at the Xinjiang Branch of the Chinese Academy of Sciences from 2009 to 2012. I earned my bachelor's degree from Harbin Institute of Technology in 2009. I was born in Harbin, China, in 1985—the city I proudly call home.\n\nLanguage Intelligence is a form of cognitive capability—shared by humans and increasingly emulated by machines—that enables agents to learn about the external world through natural language, construct highly abstract linguistic representations, and thereby understand, refine, and creatively transform that world. Our research seeks to explore and expand the frontiers of this intelligence across three interconnected domains:\n\na photo\n★ Language Modeling: The mechanism and application. I started researching language models in 2013, which was a turning point when language models shifted from n-gram approaches to neural networks [[EMNLP-2013]](https://aclanthology.org/D13-1082.pdf).\n•We have observed some interesting phenomena: [[Overthinking]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.21187), [[Chain-of-Embedding]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.13640), [[Mixed-radix Rotary Position Embedding]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.22181), etc.\n•We have proposed [[DeepMath-103K]](https://huggingface.co/datasets/zwhe99/DeepMath-103K) with Tencent, [[PolyMath]](https://huggingface.co/datasets/Qwen/PolyMath) with Qwen Team, and [[F2LLM]](https://huggingface.co/collections/codefuse-ai/f2llm) with Ant Group.\n★ Computational Linguistics: An interdisciplinary field of computer science, linguistics, cognitive science, psychology, etc.\n• We have provided the first evidence that [[Neural Theory-of-Mind Networks]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.25343) can spontaneously generalize high-order ToM, akin to human cognition.\n• We have observed that LLM can solve concrete problems through [[Meta-Reasoning]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.17820).\n★ Machine Translation (MT): I worked on MT for over ten years and will never give it up.\n• We argue that the development trend of machine translation is gradually moving toward [[Unsupervised Machine Translation]](https://wangruinlp.github.io/UNMT.pdf).\n• We are working on [[Human-like Machine Translation]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.04118) and [[Multi-agent Machine Translation]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.19118).\n\n教授课程\n\n#### Lecture\n\nCS3966: Natural Language Processing and Large Language Model (for the John Class), 2024-\nCS3602: Natural Language Processing (for the CS and AI major), 2021-\nCS438: Information Extraction, 2021-2023\nCS247: Data Mining, 2021-2022\n\n#### Tutorial\n\n[Advances and Challenges in Unsupervised Neural Machine Translation](https://wangruinlp.github.io/unmt.html).\nRui Wang and Hai Zhao\n16th conference of the European Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics (EACL-Tutorial), 2021\n[Syntax in End-to-End Natural Language Processing](https://aclanthology.org/2021.emnlp-tutorials.6/)\nHai Zhao, Rui Wang, and Kehai Chen\nThe 2021 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP-Tutorial), 2021\n[Domain Adaptation for Neural Machine Translation](https://wangruinlp.github.io/ccmt.pdf)\nChenhui Chu and Rui Wang\nThe 16th China Conference on Machine Translation (CCMT-Tutorial), 2019\n--You also refer to our survey paper in [[COLING-2018]](https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/C18-1111/)\n\n论文发表\n\n### [[Google Scholar]](https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=oTU0v5IAAAAJ&hl)\n\nRecent Representative Works\n\n[[Neural Theory-of-Mind Networks]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.25343): Spontaneous High-Order Generalization in Neural Theory-of-Mind Networks. ArXiv. 2025\n\n[[DeepMath-103K]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.11456): DeepMath-103K: A Large-Scale, Challenging, Decontaminated, and Verifiable Mathematical Dataset for Advancing Reasoning. ICLR 2026\n\n[[Overthinking]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.21187): Do NOT Think That Much for 2+3=? On the Overthinking of o1-Like LLMs. ICML.2025\n\n[[Chain-of-Embedding]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.13640): Latent Space Chain-of-Embedding Enables Output-free LLM Self-Evaluation. ICLR.2025\n\n[[Human-like Machine Translation]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.04118): Exploring Human-Like Translation Strategy with Large Language Models. TACL.2024\n\n资助项目\n\nNSFC, 62176153, Multilingual Unsupervised Machine Translation, PI, 2022-2025\nJSPS, 19K20354, Toward Unsupervised Machine Translation, PI, 2019-2020\nWe sincerely express our gratitude to Tencent, Ant Group, Alibaba, Hithink RoyalFlush, Baidu, and other companies for their generous financial support to our laboratory.\n\n获奖信息\n\n[WMT-2024](https://www2.statmt.org/wmt24/romance-task.html): 1st places in Translation into Low-Resource Languages of Spain[[Paper]](https://aclanthology.org/2024.wmt-1.92/)\n[WMT-2023](https://www2.statmt.org/wmt23/word-autocompletion.html): 1st places in Word-Level AutoCompletion[[Paper]](https://aclanthology.org/2023.wmt-1.77/)\n[WMT-2022](http://www.statmt.org/wmt22/translation-task.html): 1st places in Livonian<->English[[Paper]](https://aclanthology.org/2022.wmt-1.18/)\n[IWSLT-2022](https://wangruinlp.github.io/): 1st in the Simultaneous Speech Translation task [[Results]](https://aclanthology.org/2022.iwslt-1.10v2.pdf)[[Paper]](https://aclanthology.org/2022.iwslt-1.16/)\n[WMT-2020](http://www.statmt.org/wmt20/translation-task.html): 1st in three tasks (English->Chinese, Polish->English, and German-Upper Sorbian) [[Results]](http://matrix.statmt.org/matrix/systems_list/1920)[[Paper]](http://www.statmt.org/wmt20/pdf/2020.wmt-1.22.pdf)\n[CoNLL-2019](http://mrp.nlpl.eu/): 1st in the DM sub-task and the 2nd overall [[Results]](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/14s5Y_vM8YZ-g7O88EKnJ85c7HH1EXPQizvH3z0wDo80/edit#gid=0)[[Paper]](https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/K19-2004/)\n[WMT-2019](http://www.statmt.org/wmt19/translation-task.html): 1st in the only unsupervised MT task (German-Czech) [[Results]](http://matrix.statmt.org/matrix/systems_list/1897) [[Paper]](https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/W19-5330/)\n[WAT-2018](http://lotus.kuee.kyoto-u.ac.jp/WAT/WAT2018/index.html): 1st places in Myanmar (Burmese) <- English [[Results]](http://lotus.kuee.kyoto-u.ac.jp/WAT/evaluation/list.php?t=27&o=8)[[Paper]](https://wangruinlp.github.io/wat.pdf)\n[WMT-2018](http://www.statmt.org/wmt18/translation-task.html): 1st places in four tasks (English<->Estonian and English<->Finnish) [[Results]](https://wangruinlp.github.io/wmt-newstest18-results.pdf)[[Paper]](http://www.statmt.org/wmt18/pdf/WMT046.pdf)\n\n学术服务\n\nProgram Chair: MT Summit 2023 (Research Track)\nSenior Area Chairs: NeurIPS (2026), ACL (2024, 2026), EACL (2026), EMNLP (2025-2026), NAACL (2025)\nArea Chairs: ICML (2023-2026), NeurIPS (2022-2025), ICLR (2021-2026), EMNLP (2022), NAACL (2021), CoNLL (2021-2022), CCL (2018-2019)\nAssociate Editors: ACL Rolling Review (2024), IEICE Transactions on Information and Systems (2022-2024)\nStanding Reviewers: CL (2020-2024) and TACL (2020-2024)	\N
d299efd2-878e-4a4c-ba2d-80db07c1e2e3	ac342f75-83a2-4a42-bb9b-17642bfabf0b	https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jiaoshiml/z.html	https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jiaoshiml/z.html	cc50857e4e0b14f6c566af4deb29204e	2026-10-22 10:01:21.527753+00	200	static	utf-8	b1711039d1859732c0aa3009fc1a9f94	# 朱开元-上海交通大学计算机学院（网络空间安全学院、密码学院）\n\n[使用jAccount登录](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/user/jaccount_login.html)\n\n[English](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/en)\n\n师资队伍\n\n- ## [教师名录](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jiaoshiml.html)\n\n- ## [院士学者](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/lyys.html)\n\n- ## [国家级人才](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/gjjrc.html)\n\n- ## [兼职和双聘教师](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jzhesp.html)\n\n- ## [退休教师](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/txjiaoshi.html)\n\n- ## [人才招聘](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/rczp.html)\n\n教师名录\n\n朱开元\n\n长聘教轨副教授\n\n邮箱：kaiyuanzhu@sjtu.edu.cn\n\n地址：上海市闵行区东川路800号电院3-315\n\n所在研究所：通用人工智能研究所\n\n个人主页：[https://sjtu-cg.github.io/](https://sjtu-cg.github.io/)\n\n个人简介\n\n长聘教轨副教授，博士生导师，国家级海外青年人才，上海市海外高层次青年人才。主要研究方向为计算基因组学、癌症基因组学，聚焦基因组数据的高效存储、检索与分析，具体研究内容包括但不限于：（1）癌症基因组局部扩增与复杂结构变异（如染色体外DNA）重建；（2）基因组数据压缩与索引；（3）宏基因组、泛基因组与肿瘤微生物组分析；（4）三维基因组与染色质结构解析；（5）隐私保护基因组数据分析。我们致力于以算法创新推动基因组学研究，从海量基因组数据中挖掘生物学新规律，加深对癌症等疾病发生、发展机制的理解，加速肿瘤精准诊疗的实现。欢迎具有计算机科学、数学、统计学、生物信息学等背景的优秀学生与学者加入团队，共同开拓计算基因组学前沿。\n\n教育背景\n\n2014.09 - 2021.05 Indiana University Bloomington, Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering, 计算机科学, 博士\n2010.09 - 2014.06 山东大学, 泰山学堂, 计算机科学与技术, 本科\n\n工作履历\n\n2026.01 - 至今 上海交通大学, 计算机学院, 长聘教轨副教授\n\n2021.09 - 2025.12 UC San Diego, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, 博士后\n\n2021.03 - 2021.09 Indiana University Bloomington, Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering, 助理研究员\n\n2019.08 - 2020.12 National Cancer Institute, Cancer and Data Science Laboratory, 访问学者\n\n论文发表\n\nSome papers:\n\n1. Chowdhury, B., Zhu, K., Li, C., Alsing, J., Luebeck, J., Stefanova, M. E., Chapman, O. S., Kraft, K., Zhang, S., Lim, J. Y. S., Xie, Y., Kim, Y. J., Wu, S., Chavez, L., Nir, G., Henssen, A. G., Mischel, P. S., Chang, H. Y., & Bafna, V. (2026). Reconstructing the three-dimensional architecture of extrachromosomal DNA with ec3D. Nature Communications, 17(1), 894\n\n2. Zhu, K., Jones, M. G., Luebeck, J., Bu, X., Yi, H., Hung, K. L., Wong, I. T. L., Zhang, S., Mischel, P. S., Chang, H. Y., & Bafna, V. (2024). CoRAL accurately resolves extrachromosomal DNA genome structures with long-read sequencing. Genome Research, 34(9), 1344-1354.\n\n3. Zhu, K., Robinson, W., Schäffer, A. A., Xu, J., Ruppin, E., Ergun, A. F., Ye, Y., & Sahinalp, S. C. (2022). Strain level microbial detection and quantification with applications to single cell metagenomics. Nature Communications, 13(1), 6430\n\n4. Kockan, C., Zhu, K., Dokmai, N., Karpov, N., Kulekci, M. O., Woodruff, D. P., & Sahinalp, S. C. (2020). Sketching algorithms for genomic data analysis and querying in a secure enclave. Nature Methods, 17(3), 295-301.\n\n5. Ginart, A. A., Hui, J., Zhu, K., Numanagic, I., Courtade, T. A., Sahinalp, S. C., & Tse, D. N. (2018). Optimal compressed representation of high throughput sequence data via light assembly. Nature Communications, 9(1), 566\n\n[[Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=44g2NCsAAAAJ&hl=en)]\n\n学术服务\n\nJournal Review: Genome Research; iScience; Genome Biology; Bioinformatics; PLOS Computational Biology; IEEE/ACM Transactions on Computational Biology and Bioinformatics (TCBB); BMC Bioinformatics\n\nConference Refree: RECOMB 2025; RECOMB 2024; ISMB/ECCB 2023; RECOMB 2023; ICALP 2022; RECOMB 2022; RECOMB 2021; SIAM SOSA 2021; RECOMB 2020; RECOMB 2019; RECOMB 2018; CPM 2017\n\nProgram Committee: RECOMB-Seq 2026\n\nPosters Chair: [RECOMB 2026](https://recomb.org/recomb2026/)\n\nOrganizing Committee: [RECOMB 2022](https://recomb.org/recomb2022/index.html)	\N
94237606-1e79-423d-9ce3-cad2fd39fb55	4499bc4f-8cc5-41c6-b0d8-0eb77b5b8ba6	https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jiaoshiml/zhengweilong.html	https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jiaoshiml/zhengweilong.html	ac03cd829df9b0ab53703c27be0bcbdb	2026-10-22 10:01:50.541478+00	200	static	utf-8	2c94e41a056750087944bdc00bd9bbc4	# 郑伟龙-上海交通大学计算机学院（网络空间安全学院、密码学院）\n\n[使用jAccount登录](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/user/jaccount_login.html)\n\n[English](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/en)\n\n师资队伍\n\n- ## [教师名录](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jiaoshiml.html)\n\n- ## [院士学者](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/lyys.html)\n\n- ## [国家级人才](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/gjjrc.html)\n\n- ## [兼职和双聘教师](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jzhesp.html)\n\n- ## [退休教师](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/txjiaoshi.html)\n\n- ## [人才招聘](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/rczp.html)\n\n教师名录\n\n郑伟龙\n\n长聘教轨副教授\n\n邮箱：weilong@sjtu.edu.cn\n\n地址：上海市闵行区东川路800号电院3号楼214\n\n所在研究所：通用人工智能研究所\n\n个人主页：[https://weilongzheng.github.io/](https://weilongzheng.github.io/)\n\n个人简介\n\n郑伟龙，上海交通大学计算机学院副教授，博士生导师。入选国家级高层次海外青年人才和上海市海外高层次青年人才。麻省理工学院和哈佛大学医学院麻省总医院博士后。长期从事脑认知与智能、情感计算、脑机交互、类脑计算理论与模型和人工智能等研究。主持及参与多项国家级和省部级研究项目，包括国家自然科学基金、国家重点研发项目和上海市科委重点项目等。在国际高水平会议和期刊发表研究论文120余篇，Google学术引用超万余次，单篇被引超两千次，授权国家发明专利多项。荣获IEEE Transactions on Autonomous Mental Development最佳论文奖、IEEE Transactions on Affective Computing最佳论文奖、ACM Multimedia Top Paper奖、ARC Prize 最佳论文奖、中国人工智能学会优秀博士学位论文奖、吴文俊人工智能自然科学一等奖，入选上海市浦江人才项目、小米青年学者、微软亚洲研究院铸星计划、AI华人青年学者榜单、2023和2024年全球前2%科学家年度影响力榜单。目前担任IEEE Transactions on Affective Computing编委、教育部脑认知科学课程群虚拟教研室副主任、中国人工智能学会脑机融合与生物机器智能专委会委员、中国图象图形学学会情感计算与理解专业委员会委员、中国康复医学会脑机接口与康复专业委员会常务委员和中国认知科学学会计算神经工程专委会委员。\n\n教育背景\n\n2012.09-2018.09 上海交通大学 计算机科学与技术 工学博士\n\n2008.09-2012.06 华南理工大学 信息工程 工学学士\n\n工作履历\n\n2022.1-至今 上海交通大学计算机科学与工程系 副教授\n\n2020.10-2021.12 美国麻省理工学院MIT脑与认知科学系 博士后研究员\n\n2018.10-2020.09 美国哈佛大学医学院和麻省总医院神经病学系 博士后研究员\n\n2016.06-2016.09 日本理化学研究所脑科学中心 访问学者\n\n2014.09-2015.03 西班牙巴斯克大学计算机与人工智能系 访问学者\n\n教授课程\n\n《神经网络理论与应用》、《人工智能》、《数据科学基础》\n\n论文发表\n\n详细列表见 [Google Scholar 主页](https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=MZXXe8UAAAAJ&hl=en)\n\n1. Wei-Long Zheng, Zhongxuan Wu, Ali Hummos, Guangyu Robert Yang, and Michael M. Halassa. "Rapid context inference in a thalamocortical model using recurrent neural networks." Nature Communications 15, no. 1 (2024): 8275.\n\n2. Wei-Long Zheng, and Bao-Liang Lu. “Investigating Critical Frequency Bands and Channels for EEG- based Emotion Recognition with Deep Neural Networks.” IEEE Transactions on Autonomous Mental Development, vol. 7, no. 3, pp. 162-175, 2015. (2018 IEEE TAMD Outstanding Paper Award).\n\n3. Wei-Long Zheng, Jia-Yi Zhu, and Bao-Liang Lu. “Identifying Stable Patterns over Time for Emotion Recognition from EEG.” IEEE Transactions on Affective Computing, 10, no. 3 (2019): 417-429. (2021 IEEE TAC Best Paper Award)\n\n4. Wei-Long Zheng, Jia-Yi Zhu, Yong Peng, and Bao-Liang Lu. “EEG-Based Emotion Classification Using Deep Belief Networks.” IEEE International Conference on Multimedia and Expo (ICME’14), IEEE, 2014: 1-6.\n\n5. Wei-Long Zheng, Wei Liu, Yifei Lu, Bao-Liang Lu, and Andrzej Cichocki. “EmotionMeter: A Multimodal Framework for Recognizing Human Emotions.” IEEE Transactions on Cybernetics, 49, no. 3 (2018): 1110-1122.\n\n6. Wei-Long Zheng, Bo-Nan Dong, and Bao-Liang Lu. “Multimodal Emotion Recognition using EEG and Eye Tracking Data.” 36th Annual International Conference of the IEEE Engineering in Medicine and Biology Society (EMBC’14), IEEE, 2014: 5040-5043.\n\n7. Wei-Long Zheng and Bao-Liang Lu. “A multimodal approach to estimating vigilance using EEG and forehead EOG.” Journal of Neural Engineering, 14(2): 026017, 2017.\n\n8. Yifei Lu*, Wei-Long Zheng*, Binbin Li, and Bao-Liang Lu. “Combining Eye Movements and EEG to Enhance Emotion Recognition.” in Proc. of the International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI’15), 2015:1170-1176. (*contributed equally as joint first authors).\n\n9. Wei-Long Zheng and Bao-Liang Lu. “Personalizing EEG-based Affective Models with Transfer Learning.” in Proc. of the 25th International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI), 2016: 2732- 3738.\n\n10. Wei-Long Zheng, Kunpeng Gao, Gang Li, Wei Liu, Chao Liu, Jing-Quan Liu, Guoxing Wang, Bao- Liang Lu. “Vigilance Estimation Using a Wearable EOG Device in Real Driving Environment.” IEEE Transactions on Intelligent Transportation Systems, 21, no. 1 (2019): 170-184.\n\n11. Wei-Long Zheng, Haoqi Sun, Oluwaseun Akeju, M Brandon Westover. “Adaptive Sedation Monitoring from EEG in ICU Patients with Online Learning.” IEEE Transactions on Biomedical Engineering, 67, no. 6 (2019): 1696-1706.\n\n资助项目\n\n国家自然科学基金面上项目, 62376158, 自然场景的多模态情感脑机接口实验范式及计算模型研究, 2024年01月至 2027年12月，主持\n\n获奖信息\n\n2025年 ARC Prize 最佳论文奖\n\n2022年 ACM Multimedia Top Paper奖\n\n2021年 IEEE Transactions on Affective Computing 最佳论文奖\n\n2021年 吴文俊人工智能自然科学奖 一等奖\n\n2018年 中国人工智能学会优秀博士学位论文奖\n\n2018年 上海交通大学优秀博士学位论文提名\n\n2018年 IEEE Transactions on Autonomous Mental Development 优秀论文奖\n\n学术服务\n\nIEEE Transactions on Affective Computing编委、《Cyborg and Bionic Systems》青年编委、教育部脑认知科学课程群虚拟教研室副主任、中国人工智能学会脑机融合与生物机器智能专委会委员、中国图象图形学学会情感计算与理解专业委员会委员、中国康复医学会脑机接口与康复专业委员会常务委员和中国认知科学学会计算神经工程专委会委员	\N
7d87f366-37ae-41f9-a242-a08c0a33b5a4	8f2e72c3-dd81-4f74-a212-250869a4d580	https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jiaoshiml/qiuweidong.html	https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jiaoshiml/qiuweidong.html	caa6cf24cc62085b885a4937252c9039	2026-10-22 10:02:20.591193+00	200	static	utf-8	ffa363007a6668743c86a07ec785711e	# 邱卫东-上海交通大学计算机学院（网络空间安全学院、密码学院）\n\n[使用jAccount登录](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/user/jaccount_login.html)\n\n[English](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/en)\n\n师资队伍\n\n- ## [教师名录](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jiaoshiml.html)\n\n- ## [院士学者](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/lyys.html)\n\n- ## [国家级人才](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/gjjrc.html)\n\n- ## [兼职和双聘教师](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/jzhesp.html)\n\n- ## [退休教师](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/txjiaoshi.html)\n\n- ## [人才招聘](https://www.cs.sjtu.edu.cn/rczp.html)\n\n教师名录\n\n邱卫东\n\n长聘教授\n\n邮箱：qiuwd@sjtu.edu.cn\n\n所在研究所：网络空间安全研究所\n\n个人简介\n\n长聘教授/博士生导师，中国中文信息学会大数据与隐私计算专委会副主任委员、ACM SIGSAC CHINA技术委员会委员、电子学会高级会员、国家移动信息产业技术创新战略联盟网络特种技术专业委员会专家，入选教育部“新世纪优秀人才计划”、上海市优秀技术带头人，荣获中央网信办全国网络安全优秀教师。\n\n长期从事密码分析/密码工程、数据要素共享流通安全、大数据隐私保护等方向的研究工作，先后主持了“十四五”国家重点研发计划项目（首席科学家）、131专项集成验证项目、“十三五”国家重点研发计划课题、国家科技部863专项项目、国家自然科学基金等多项国家项目，在TIFS、TDSC、IJCAI、CSCW、CHI、FSE发表论文150余篇，研究成果荣获上海市科技进步一等奖、上海市计算机学会科技进步一等奖。\n\n教育背景\n\n2001.11-2004.01，德国哈根大学，博士后\n\n1998.02-2001.07，上海交通大学，计算机软件与理论，博士\n\n1995.09-1998.02，西安电子科技大学，密码学，硕士\n\n1991.09-1995.07，西安电子科技大学，应用数学，学士\n\n工作履历\n\n2004-至今，上海交通大学计算机学院（网络空间安全学院），教授/博导\n\n教授课程\n\n本科专业必修课程：现代密码学\n\n研究生课程：密码协议\n\n论文发表\n\n1. Guowei Ling, Peng Tang, Jinyong Shan, Fei Tang, Weidong Qiu,“More Efficient, Privacy-Enhanced, and Powerful Privacy-Preserving Feature Retrieval Private Set Intersection,” Transactions on Information Forensics and Security (TIFS), 2025.\n\n2. Guowei Ling, Peng Tang, Fei Tang, Shifeng Sun, Shouling Ji, Weidong Qiu, “Ultra-Fast Private Set Intersection from Efficient Oblivious Key-Value Stores,” IEEE Transactions on Dependable and Secure Computing (TDSC), 2025.\n\n3. Peng Tang, Xiaoyu Zhu, Weidong Qiu, Zheng Huang, Zhenyu Mu, Shujun Li, “FLAD: Byzantine-Robust Federated Learning Based on Gradient Feature Anomaly Detection,” IEEE Transactions on Dependable and Secure Computing (TDSC), 2025.\n\n4. Yangde Wang, Weidong Qiu, Peng Tang, Hao Tian, Shujun Li, “SE#PCFG: Semantically Enhanced PCFG for Password Analysis and Cracking,” IEEE Transactions on Dependable and Secure Computing (TDSC), 2025.\n\n5. Yuqi Niu, Weidong Qiu, Peng Tang, Lifan Wang, Shuo Chen, Shujun Li, Nadin Kökciyan, Ben Niu, "Everyone's Privacy Matters! An Analysis of Privacy Leakage from Real-World Facial Images on Twitter and Associated User Behaviors," 28th ACM Conference on Computer-Supported Cooperative Work and Social Computing (CSCW), 2025.\n\n6. Yuqi Niu, Nicole Meng-Schneider, Weidong Qiu, Nadin Kökciyan, “‘I am not the primary focus’-Understanding the Perspectives of Bystanders in Photos Shared Online," 2025 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems (CHI), 2025.\n\n7. Guowei Ling, Fei Tang, Chaochao Cai, Jinyong Shan, Haiyang Xue, Wulu Li, Peng Tang, Xinyi Huang, and Weidong Qiu, “P2FRPSI: Privacy-Preserving Feature Retrieved Private Set Intersection,” IEEE Transactions on Information Forensics and Security (TIFS), vol. 19, pp. 2201-2216, 2024.\n\n8. Ke Hu, Peng Tang, Liyao Xiang, and Weidong Qiu, “Feature Norm Regularized Federated Learning: Utilizing Data Disparities for Model Performance Gains,” IJCAI 2024.\n\n9. Jianfei Sun, yangyang bao, Weidong Qiu, Rongxing Lu, Songnian Zhang, Yunguo Guan, Xiaochun Cheng, “Privacy-preserving Fine-grained Data Sharing with Dynamic Service for the Cloud-edge IoT,” IEEE Transactions on Dependable and Secure Computing (TDSC), 2024.\n\n10. Fei Tang, Guowei Ling, Chaochao Cai, Jinyong Shan, Xuanqi Liu, Peng Tang, Weidong Qiu. “Solving Small Exponential ECDLP in EC-Based Additively Homomorphic Encryption and Applications,” IEEE Transactions on Information Forensics and Security (TIFS), vol. 18, pp. 3517-3530, 2023.\n\n11. Huina Li, Le He, Shiyao Chen, Jian Guo, Weidong Qiu, “Automatic Preimage Attack Framework on Ascon Using a Linearize-and-Guess Approach,” IACR Transactions on Symmetric Cryptology (FSE), 2023.\n\n12. Guozhen Liu, Weidong Qiu, and Yi Tu, “New Techniques for Searching Differential Trails in Keccak,” IACR Transactions on Symmetric Cryptology (FSE), 2019.\n\n资助项目\n\n1. “十四五”国家重点研发计划项目，“面向数据可信确权与交易的安全保障技术”（编号：2023YFB3106500）, 2023.12-2026.11，主持\n\n2. 131专项集成验证项目， "网络空间自主对抗关键技术研究及验证平台搭建"，2024.12-2025.12，主持\n\n3. “十三五”国家重点研发计划课题， “电子凭据体系安全监测与追溯处置关键技术及系统”（编号：2017YFB0802704），2017.07-2020.12，主持\n\n4. 国家自然基金项目，“基于内部置换差分分析的sha3安全性研究”（编号61972249），2020.1-2023.12，主持\n\n5. 上海交大-太保人工智能联合实验室，2021-2023，共同创建人\n\n获奖信息\n\n1、上海市科技进步一等奖\n\n2、中央网信办全国网络安全优秀教师\n\n3、上海市计算学会科技进步一等奖\n\n4、上海交通大学教书育人三等奖\n\n5、上海市教学成果二等奖\n\n6、上海市优秀技术带头人\n\n7、教育部“新世纪优秀人才支持计划”\n\n学术服务\n\n1、中国中文信息学会大数据与隐私计算专委会副主任委员\n\n2、ACM SIGSAC CHINA技术委员会委员\n\n3、IEEE PCDS 2024 & 2023 Co-Chair; PriCom 2019 Co-Chair; PriCom 2018 Organization Chair; PriCom 2017 TPC\n\n4、TIFS、TDSC、Information Sciences、Computers & Security 等多个国内外学术期刊评审人	\N
