cmupmebvw00rtsopiqcngltrx	cmupmeb3t00rcsopiq31mbr6t	Recent advances in ceramic matrix composites for electromagnetic interference shielding: Mechanisms, components and structural design	2026	\N	\N	\N	: Electromagnetic interference issues are becoming increasingly prominent in high-frequency communication, aerospace, and high-temperature electronic systems, placing higher demands on the lightweight, high-temperature resistance, structural stability, and broadband electromagnetic shielding effectiveness of shielding materials. Ceramic matrix composites have become important candidate materials for electromagnetic shielding in extreme environments due to their excellent thermal stability, oxidation resistance, and mechanical properties. However, most ceramic matrices have low intrinsic electrical conductivity, requiring the introduction of conductive reinforcement phases, interface regulation, and multi-scale structural design to achieve effective electromagnetic wave attenuation. This article systematically reviews the electromagnetic shielding mechanisms of ceramic matrix composites, focusing on the analysis of the effects of reinforcements, interface layers, and ceramic matrices on conductive loss, polarization loss, magnetic loss, and impedance matching, and summarizes structural design strategies such as gradient, multilayer, porous, sandwich, and segregated structures. Final	https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jmrt.2026.08.006	W7172452135	\N	https://openalex.org/W7172452135	2026-10-01 14:19:14.733	2026-10-05 05:37:18.161
