cmupmu70c015jta0y9obaw1a6	cmupmu6ao0154ta0yhzyfrrfk	LightOpt: Lights Optimization for Real-time Rendering	2026	\N	\N	\N	Modern game scenes often require hundreds of lights to achieve rich visual detail, yet evaluating many lights per pixel remains a major performance bottleneck in real-time rendering, especially on low-end platforms. We present a differentiable lighting optimization pipeline that automatically reduces the number of active lights while preserving the final rendered appearance. Our method jointly optimizes light parameters and dynamically performs light removal, merging, and insertion during optimization. We introduce two loss functions to minimize redundant light overlap and prevent under-illumination, and extend our approach to support Time-of-Day lighting. Experiments on production game scenes show that our method reduces lighting cost by 18–52% while consistently outperforming artist-authored light reductions in visual fidelity.	https://doi.org/10.1145/3799902.3811072	W7168650359	\N	https://openalex.org/W7168650359	2026-10-01 14:31:34.909	2026-10-01 14:31:34.909
