cmuqpmem9006b13pgc54r2vgk	cmuqpmdpn005w13pgq3m2p6y6	Precision Studies and Searches for C P Asymmetries in the Inclusive Decay Λ c + → Λ X	2026	\N	\N	\N	Based on e + e − annihilation data collected with the BESIII detector at center-of-mass energies from 4.600 to 4.699 GeV, corresponding to an integrated luminosity of 4.5 fb − 1 , we present the first measurement of the longitudinal polarization of Λ hyperon produced in the inclusive decay Λ c + → Λ X , where X denotes any allowed final states. The polarizations are determined to be P Λ = − 0.393 ± 0.05 5 stat ± 0.02 0 syst and P Λ ¯ = 0.288 ± 0.05 6 stat ± 0.01 7 syst . A search for C P violation is performed using an asymmetry constructed from the Λ polarization and the Λ → p π − decay asymmetry parameter, and A C P pol = 0.15 ± 0.1 2 stat ± 0.0 3 syst was obtained. Furthermore, an updated measurement of the absolute branching fraction is reported as B ( Λ c + → Λ X ) = ( 38.07 ± 0.3 8 stat ± 0.4 9 syst ) % , representing a fourfold precision improvement over the previous BESIII measurement. A search for C P violation in the decay rate yields A C P dir = ( 1.5 ± 1.0 stat ± 1.0 syst ) % . No evidence for C P violation is observed in this inclusive charm baryon deca	https://doi.org/10.1103/cxm9-mr48	W7203727582	\N	https://openalex.org/W7203727582	2026-10-02 08:37:16.545	2026-10-03 10:58:06.332
