cmuqprwpz00pjf79cggxea7t1	cmuqprvk200p8f79c2nc0mgkn	Analysis of Coal Mine Safety Accident Risk Intervention Propagation Based on Agent Heterogeneity: Considering Intervention Time and Risk Preference	2026	\N	\N	\N	ABSTRACT Complex nonlinear relationships exist among coal mine accident risks, which provide favorable conditions for risk propagation. Insufficient identification and prevention of these risks can easily trigger chain reactions among risk factors and eventually lead to accidents. To accurately locate risk intervention nodes, this study took coal mine accident cases that occurred in China from 2020 to 2024 as the research object. By integrating association rule mining and complex network methods, a risk interaction network for coal mine accidents was constructed, and the interaction strengths among risks were quantified. Furthermore, factors such as risk concealment, personnel risk preference, risk propagation intensity, and risk intervention timing were introduced to improve the traditional SEIR risk propagation model. The entire process of coal mine accident risk propagation was then simulated. The main findings are as follows: (1) For every 5 s that risk intervention is advanced, the spread of risk propagation can be reduced by 23.7%, and the risk network can return to a stable state earlier. (2) Personnel risk preference significantly affects the peak value of risk propagation 	https://doi.org/10.1002/qre.70388	W7212025349	\N	https://openalex.org/W7212025349	2026-10-02 08:41:33.288	2026-10-05 05:27:25.509
