cmuqpv87n01cif79cj1vh56uk	cmuqpv6z601c1f79csii1iz7z	Online detection of transformer rated capacity based on data fitting	2026	\N	\N	\N	This paper proposes a method for determining the short-circuit impedance of a transformer based on data fitting techniques, which is further used to derive the transformer’s rated capacity. By establishing an equivalent circuit model and performing linear fitting on measured voltage and current data, the short-circuit impedance of three-phase distribution transformers can be calculated with reasonable accuracy. A simulation analysis is conducted on a 100 kVA dual-winding three-phase transformer. The results show that the calculated short-circuit impedance has a small error compared to the nameplate value, and the derived capacity aligns well with expectations, verifying the feasibility and accuracy of the proposed method. Compared with traditional offline testing methods, this technique does not require power outages and has the potential for online implementation. This study provides a new and effective approach for on-site identification and condition monitoring of the rated capacity of distribution transformers.	https://doi.org/10.3389/fenrg.2026.1751219	W7153093922	\N	https://openalex.org/W7153093922	2026-10-02 08:44:08.147	2026-10-05 05:42:00.263
cmuqpv9vn01ctf79cizvbl0cu	cmuqpv8f201ckf79cnfdf2vj2	Glutamine sequestration promotes tumor growth and immune evasion through elevation of arginine methylation in hepatocellular carcinoma	2026	\N	\N	\N	Abstract Mechanisms underlying the immunosuppressive microenvironment in hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC) extend beyond immune checkpoints to include metabolic competition. Here, we identify a metabolic evasion pathway driven by SLC1A5 overexpression, which enables HCC cells to sequester glutamine from the tumor microenvironment (TME). This influx sustains the intracellular methionine availability, driving pro-tumorigenic arginine hypermethylation, while simultaneously depleting extracellular glutamine required for cytotoxic CD8+ T cell effector function. This creates a dual mechanism of progression: intrinsic epigenetic activation and extrinsic immune starvation. We propose a synergistic strategy co-targeting glutamine transport (V9302) and arginine methylation (AdOx). In vivo, this regimen induced tumor cytotoxicity and restored T cell function, eliciting a robust anti-tumor response. These findings identify a glutamine–arginine methylation axis as a critical link between metabolic reprogramming and immune evasion in HCC, offering a rationale for metabolic-epigenetic co-targeting therapies.	https://doi.org/10.1038/s41419-026-09267-y	W7213368803	\N	https://openalex.org/W7213368803	2026-10-02 08:44:10.308	2026-10-05 05:42:01.97
