cmuqpwjaf01o5f79cqsuglm03	cmuqpwhqa01nof79cp7zzscdi	Dynamic Autonomy Allocation for Human-Multi-UAV Cooperative Inspection Based on Deep Reinforcement Learning with Cognitive Load Constraints	2026	\N	\N	\N	In multi-UAV cooperative inspection tasks, a single operator must supervise multiple UAVs simultaneously, leading to significant cognitive workload challenges. Existing methods typically assign fixed autonomy levels, which cannot adapt to dynamic mission conditions. To address this issue, this paper formulates the autonomy allocation problem as a constrained Markov Decision Process and proposes a Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO)-based method with explicit cognitive load constraints. A composite reward function is designed to jointly optimize task completion efficiency, UAV survivability, and operator workload management. A simulation environment with heterogeneous task difficulty and probabilistic inspection outcomes is developed to create meaningful trade-offs among three autonomy levels. Experimental results show that the proposed method achieves a mean reward of 130.8 with a cognitive load of 0.349 within the optimal range, outperforming the ablation variant without cognitive constraints (122.7, cognitive load 0.566) and the fixed-rule baseline (123.5, cognitive load 0.130).	https://doi.org/10.3233/faia260658	W7204519910	\N	https://openalex.org/W7204519910	2026-10-02 08:45:09.159	2026-10-05 05:48:58.262
cmuqpxbzr01uhf79cl5pqj59q	cmuqpxajt01u6f79c3m1kpdtv	Scaling Properties of Text Conditioning in Visual Generation	2026	\N	\N	\N	We study empirical scaling properties for text conditioning in visual generation. Such properties have rarely been measured because diffusion loss does not scale with the number of tokens in natural-language prompts. Surprisingly, we find that the converged diffusion loss scales with the amount of structured language in the prompt. To quantify structured language, we adapt two complementary measures: a white-box likelihood metric (GPG) and a black-box attribute metric (ED). Across controlled training runs, the converged diffusion loss decreases approximately linearly with GPG and follows a power law with ED. Guided by these scaling properties, we improve \\emph{diffusability} by constructing structured prompts with semantic and geometric annotations derived from images, and improve \\emph{promptability} by training a prompter through supervised fine-tuning, cold-start, and verifier-gated on-policy distillation. The resulting system outperforms all evaluated open-weight models on nearly every compositional, reasoning, and world-knowledge benchmark, while matching or surpassing the strongest closed-weight models on most evaluations.	\N	W7172473853	\N	https://openalex.org/W7172473853	2026-10-02 08:45:46.36	2026-10-05 05:49:29.969
