cmusa11v8015z6ojwmddiex0i	cmusa111y015q6ojwgio8gksm	Large-size magnon cat states through intrinsic three-magnon nonlinearity	2026	\N	\N	\N	The cat state, as an important tool for exploring the classical-quantum boundary, not only provides important tests of macroscopic quantum effects, but also has important applications in quantum metrology and quantum computation. The three-magnon process, which originates from the magnetic dipole-dipole interaction, has been less explored in the preparation of nonclassical magnon state. Here, we develop the magnon parametric coupling process that arises from the three-magnon scattering. The magnon parametric coupling strength is analytically derived and can reach a strong coupling regime within a discretized magnon mode system. Based on this, we propose a scheme to prepare the cat state without involving external nonlinearity in a magnetic system. Through the magnon parametric coupling, the extra magnon dissipation channel provided by the magnon-photon interaction induces an effective two-magnon loss channel, thereby steering the magnon into the cat state manifold. Notably, the size of the magnon cat state is inversely proportional to the parametric coupling strength, which facilitates the preparation of large-size cat states, even under environmental decoherence. Our work opens a 	https://doi.org/10.1103/hmf4-19vq	W7170554739	\N	https://openalex.org/W7170554739	2026-10-03 10:56:18.356	2026-10-05 05:28:13.039
cmusa11vz01636ojwnel2s88q	cmusa111y015q6ojwgio8gksm	Improved artificial lemming optimization algorithm for UAVs application	2025	\N	\N	\N	Unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) are confronted the challenges of intricate terrain, dynamic obstacles and multiple constraints when they conduct the path planning in complex environments. Traditional algorithms suffer from slow convergence and local optima. Artificial lemming algorithm simulates the lemming behavior to achieve the optimization, but its global exploration and local exploitation capabilities require the improvement. In view of these problems, we propose an improved artificial lemming optimization algorithm (IALOA), which is optimized by four strategies: enhancing the diversity of initial population using Latin hypercube sampling; designing adaptive spiral position update strategy to reduce the search fluctuations in exploitation stage, introducing sine random strategy to dynamically adjust the search step size and using the Gaussian mutation strategy to strengthen the ability to escape from local optima. IALOA ranks first in all dimensions of CEC2017 benchmark test, and it has high efficiency and stability. IALOA is an effective solution for UAV path planning, when planning the shortest path in 3D path planning simulation for UAVs, it exhibits stronger obstacle avoid	https://doi.org/10.1117/12.3093009	W4417452032	\N	https://openalex.org/W4417452032	2026-10-03 10:56:18.383	2026-10-05 05:28:13.055
cmusa11w701656ojwgfm1u268	cmusa111y015q6ojwgio8gksm	Magnon-induced exceptional point and enhanced sensing via Brillouin scattering	2024	\N	\N	\N	In recent years, cavity optomagnonics has received considerable research interest, and the notions drawn from non-Hermitian physics have also attracted attention. Based on Faraday effect and Cotton-Mouton effect, we theoretically propose a scheme to realize exceptional point (EP) in a cavity optomagnonic system. The scheme relies on Brillouin scattering (BLS), i.e., a triple-frequency resonance between the excited photon and magnon inside cavity. By exploring the dependence of the exceptional points on the system parameters, we show that the proposed EP is magnetically tunable. Regarding the applications of the magnon-induced EP, we further discuss the greatly enhanced sensitivity, which responds to two kinds of perturbation near or on the exceptional point. Moreover, we show that the tunable EP can guard against the cavity defect to maintain the optimal precision. Characterized by the mentioned features, our proposal offers a further understanding of non-Hermitian cavity optomagnonics, and it has potential in the applications for high-sensitivity quantum sensing.	https://doi.org/10.1364/ol.542203	W4404227763	\N	https://openalex.org/W4404227763	2026-10-03 10:56:18.391	2026-10-05 05:28:13.063
