cmusaf8fc03sq6ojwmaznh9rh	cmusaf7e303sh6ojwfsiqzf00	Onsager principle The basic and useful principle in soft matter physics	2026	\N	\N	\N	Abstract Onsager principle is the principle proposed by Lars Onsager in 1931 in his second paper on the reciprocal relation. The principle formed the core of the classical irreversible thermodynamics. It is particularly important in soft matter physics, since most phenomena taking place in soft matter obey this principle, and existing kinetic equations are derived from this principle. The principle is also useful as a tool for solving problems. Like Lagrangean in classical mechanics, it gives flexibility in choosing coordinate system, and helps up to derive governing equations to be solved. Furthermore, being a minimum principle, it provides various ways of finding the solution, i.e., the minimum. Here I review this important and useful principle from a practical view point emphasizing what it is, how it works and how to use it.	https://doi.org/10.1088/1674-1056/ae8db0	W7169884289	\N	https://openalex.org/W7169884289	2026-10-03 11:07:20.04	2026-10-03 11:07:20.04
