cmusajylf04vm6ojw0xuj1o79	cmusajxpu04v96ojwkieml1ci	Lightweight real-time detection of sweet potato virus disease by a hybrid CNN–Transformer network	2026	\N	\N	\N	Timely and precise detection of sweet potato virus disease (SPVD) is essential for ensuring crop health and improving yield quality in precision agriculture. However, conventional deep learning models often struggle to capture subtle lesion features under complex field conditions. This paper proposes Swin-SPVDNet, a hybrid CNN-Transformer detection framework with task-specific architectural enhancements that combines convolutional neural networks (CNNs) with a modified Swin Transformer to effectively integrate local spatial details and global contextual information. Unlike conventional hybrid models that simply stack convolutional and transformer blocks, the proposed network introduces three key structural designs: (1) A C2PSA-enhanced convolutional backbone for improved local feature sensitivity. (2) A C3STR module that tightly integrates convolutional operations with Swin Transformer blocks for joint local–global feature interaction. (3) A Residual Attention Block (RAB) that refines feature representations while stabilizing gradient propagation. A field-collected SPVD image dataset was constructed using handheld RGB imaging under real agricultural conditions. Extensive experiment	https://doi.org/10.1016/j.compag.2026.112319	W7204154634	\N	https://openalex.org/W7204154634	2026-10-03 11:11:00.579	2026-10-03 11:11:00.579
