cmuusy17f00q38xwwttf5jxg4	cmuusy09y00pu8xww6059x5z5	A measurement-operator framework for generative reconstruction of flow fields from sparse and indirect sensing	2026	\N	\N	\N	Inferring high-fidelity continuous flow fields from scattered and indirect sensor data, such as scanning LiDAR projections, poses a highly ill-posed inverse problem. While deep generative models provide expressive priors, existing architectures rely on uniform grids and direct masking, severely restricting their utility for off-grid and projected observations. We introduce measurement-operator flow matching (MOFM), a grid-free generative framework that natively assimilates diverse sensing modalities via a point-cloud conditioner. During inference, composable and retraining-free sampling guidance imposes measurement consistency, alongside strict divergence-free constraints for genuinely incompressible conditions. To ensure stable optimization across diverse flow regimes, a unified per-component normalization prevents massive ambient advection from washing out small-scale turbulent signatures. Evaluated on a canonical Kolmogorov flow and a complex wind-turbine wake, MOFM substantially reduces reconstruction error compared to parameter-matched baselines, faithfully preserving both the spatial velocity fields and the high-frequency turbulent energy spectrum.	https://doi.org/10.1016/j.taml.2026.100741	W7213327937	\N	https://openalex.org/W7213327937	2026-10-05 05:21:22.587	2026-10-05 05:21:22.587
