cmuut2al501xa8xww4z525ywg	cmuut29nb01wt8xww5si7d5tz	Feature-Foundation Model Evolution: Toward Large-Model-Empowered Low-Latency Semantic Communication	2026	\N	\N	\N	To meet stringent requirements of high throughput in the 6G era, semantic communication (SC), a revolutionary framework that transmits semantic information rather than the original data, is expected to be a promising solution. However, existing SC frameworks struggle to accommodate data with new semantic features effectively and ensure minimal data processing latency. This is because achieving strong adaptability necessitates large-scale foundation models, such as large language models with robust semantic understanding, whereas low latency demands small models with simple structures. To address this issue, we propose a feature-foundation model evolution framework toward large model-empowered low-latency SC. In this framework, small-scale feature models and large-scale foundation models are deployed at edge nodes and cloud servers, respectively. The feature models perform real-time semantic encoding and decoding, and they evolve with the aid of foundation models when data with new semantic features occur, thus assuring low latency and high generalization ability simultaneously. We detail the architecture of the proposed collaborative framework and the related evolution protocol. Mo	https://doi.org/10.1109/mvt.2026.3653098	W7127156663	\N	https://openalex.org/W7127156663	2026-10-05 05:24:41.37	2026-10-05 05:24:41.37
