cmuutve06070t8xwwy0bzudul	cmuutvd61070e8xwwsr4mwku3	A quadratic neural network for multiphase flow prediction in CO 2 sequestration	2026	\N	\N	\N	Abstract Geological carbon sequestration (GCS) is widely recognized as a key strategy for mitigating global climate change by reducing atmospheric CO 2 concentrations. Deep learning methods, such as long short-term memory (LSTM) networks and multilayer perceptron (MLP) models, have been widely applied to multiphase flow prediction in CO 2 sequestration. However, most existing deep learning approaches struggle to capture complex nonlinear dynamics, making it challenging to achieve both high prediction accuracy and computational efficiency in large-scale scenarios. To address this limitation, a quadratic multi-layer perceptron (Quadratic-MLP) is proposed by introducing a quadratic polynomial input–output mapping at the neuron level, which enhances nonlinear representation capability while maintaining a compact network architecture. The proposed Quadratic-MLP is applied to multiphase flow prediction in CO 2 sequestration using 27 numerical simulation cases generated from three heterogeneous geological models, with a spatial resolution of 25 × 25 × 3 over 72 time steps. Results demonstrate that the Quadratic-MLP outperforms conventional LSTM and MLP models. Compared with the convention	https://doi.org/10.1088/1402-4896/ae9ce8	W7203919616	\N	https://openalex.org/W7203919616	2026-10-05 05:47:18.823	2026-10-05 05:47:18.823
