cmuutw5i307848xwwjslxhkrk	cmuutw2oa077n8xwwf34il2bu	Robust topology optimization for fracture resistance based on fracture phase field and interval model	2026	\N	\N	\N	A novel robust topology optimization framework is proposed for designing fracture-resistant structures under multi-source uncertainty in loads and material parameters. The framework integrates the fracture phase field model with an interval model to quantify uncertainty. The upper and lower bounds of the structural resistance to external forces are established as robustness indicators and serve as the optimization objectives. To address the challenge that the nonlinear and potentially non-monotonic response of these forces to uncertain parameters obscures the feasible resistance bounds, the interval collocation method is employed to efficiently resolve this feasible region. Adjoint-based sensitivity analysis is derived for the robustness indicators within the phase field formulation. Three numerical examples demonstrate the validity and reliability of the proposed method in yielding designs with enhanced and consistent fracture resistance under uncertainty.	https://doi.org/10.1016/j.advengsoft.2026.104196	W4416078137	\N	https://openalex.org/W4416078137	2026-10-05 05:47:54.459	2026-10-05 05:47:54.459
