cmuutwvvu07he8xwwnns8gzaf	cmuutu6hk06l58xwwgy7bo058	TrojanGPL: Vulnerability Analysis and Mitigation of Backdoor Attacks on Graph Prompt Learning	2026	\N	\N	\N	Graph Prompt Learning (GPL) effectively bridges the gap between graph pre-training and downstream tasks, addressing the bottleneck in knowledge transfer. However, its susceptibility to backdoor attacks during pre-training remains largely unexplored. This work systematically investigates the backdoor risks in GPL and introducesTrojanGPL-a cross-context backdoor attack that embeds triggers solely through manipulations of the pre-trained encoder, independent of downstream knowledge. Our analysis reveals that jointly optimizing trigger graphs with the prompt mechanism not only narrows the gap between upstream and downstream main tasks but also aligns main and backdoor learning objectives, facilitating seamless backdoor transfer from pre-trained models to diverse downstream applications. To counter this threat, we proposeES-Detector, a defense mechanism that identifies backdoored graph samples by detecting discriminative embedding shifts upon the removal of important nodes. Specifically, when clean and backdoored graphs are predicted as the same class, clean graphs exhibit stable embedding changes, whereas backdoored graphs show significant deviations from clean ones. Extensive experime	https://doi.org/10.1109/tdsc.2026.3702151	W7164204182	\N	https://openalex.org/W7164204182	2026-10-05 05:48:28.65	2026-10-05 05:48:28.65
cmuutwvw207hg8xwwya2z9o55	cmuutu6hk06l58xwwgy7bo058	SGA: Self-boosting Attributed Graph Alignment via Neighborhood Consistency-based Edge Enhancement	2026	\N	\N	\N	Graph alignment, the task of identifying corresponding nodes across different graphs, is crucial for applications ranging from social network analysis to bioinformatics. Although most existing methods leverage graph neural networks (GNNs) to learn node embeddings for attributed graphs and match them based on node similarity, they often rely on objectives designed for node classification or link prediction. These approaches preserve node proximity within individual graphs but fail to capture cross-graph correspondence knowledge, leading to suboptimal alignment performance.	https://doi.org/10.1145/3770854.3780180	W7171994310	\N	https://openalex.org/W7171994310	2026-10-05 05:48:28.658	2026-10-05 05:48:28.658
